WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.075
Who decides?

2
00:00:01.075 --> 00:00:05.061
The partner and the agency each
carry part of every activity,

3
00:00:05.061 --> 00:00:10.163
from affiliation and proofing to
lifecycle, incident response and evidence.

4
00:00:10.163 --> 00:00:14.585
On the agency side there is one decider
per row: the agency business owner,

5
00:00:14.585 --> 00:00:18.787
the official accountable for the
program the partner persons serve.

6
00:00:18.787 --> 00:00:23.325
The title is provisional, and the
record names a person, not a title.

7
00:00:23.325 --> 00:00:27.401
The sponsor, usually the program
manager who works with the partner,

8
00:00:27.401 --> 00:00:31.696
vouches for its people, reviews their
access and requests suspensions,

9
00:00:31.696 --> 00:00:34.025
but never approves their own requests.

10
00:00:34.025 --> 00:00:38.750
The identity governance officer owns the
list of approved partner organizations.

11
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.288
Two rows need comment.

12
00:00:40.288 --> 00:00:43.336
In a live incident, security
operations contains

13
00:00:43.336 --> 00:00:45.938
first and the business
owner is told after.

14
00:00:45.938 --> 00:00:49.774
And going to production has one
decider with a required consult:

15
00:00:49.774 --> 00:00:52.813
the authorizing official's
input must be on record.

16
00:00:52.813 --> 00:00:57.453
A consult isn't a second approval, but an
objection the business owner overrides

17
00:00:57.453 --> 00:01:01.870
becomes a risk acceptance, and that is
the authorizing official's decision.
